  "term": "McCarthy Scales of Children’s Abilities",
  "definition": "The McCarthy Scales of Children’s Abilities is a cognitive test used to assess and track children’s development from about 2.5 to 8.5 years of age. A short form is described as easy to administer in busy clinical settings and has been used with school-age children.",
